hadiths[25]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16283","He said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yala ibn Ata informed us from Waki ibn Udus from his paternal uncle Abu Razin, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The dream is upon the foot of a bird as long as it is not interpreted; when it is interpreted it occurs. He said: And the dream is a part of forty-six parts of prophethood. He said: And I think he said: Let him tell it only to a loving one or one of judgment."
"16284","Bahz narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Yala ibn Ata from Waki ibn Udus from his paternal uncle Abu Razin from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The dream is suspended on the foot of a bird as long as its companion does not speak of it; when he speaks of it, it occurs. And do not speak of it except to a scholar or an adviser or an intelligent one. And the righteous dream is a part of forty parts of prophethood."
"16285","Waki narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us from al-Numan ibn Salim from Amr ibn Aws from Abu Razin al-Uqayli that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My father is a very old man unable to perform Hajj or Umrah or to travel. He said: Perform Hajj for your father and Umrah."
"16286","He said: It was narrated to us."
"16287","He said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah informed us from Yala ibn Ata from Waki ibn Udus from his paternal uncle Abu Razin, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, will all of us see Allah, Mighty and Majestic is He, on the Day of Resurrection, and what is the sign of that in His creation? He said: O Abu Razin, does not each of you see the moon alone with him? He said: I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Then Allah is greater."
"16288","He said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah informed us from Yala ibn Ata from Waki ibn Udus from his paternal uncle Abu Razin, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Our Lord laughs at the despair of His servant and the nearness of change. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, does the Lord, Mighty and Majestic is He, laugh? He said: Yes. He said: We shall never lack good from a Lord who laughs."
"16289","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah informed us from Yala ibn Ata from Waki ibn Udus from his paternal uncle Abu Razin, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, where was our Lord, Mighty and Majestic is He, before He created His creation? He said: He was in mist with no air beneath it and no air above it, then He created His Throne upon the water."
"16290","He said: Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us from Yala ibn Ata from Waki ibn Udus from Abu Razin, his uncle, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, where is my mother? He said: Your mother is in the Fire. He said: I said: Then where are those of your family who passed? He said: Are you not pleased that your mother be with my mother? My father said: The correct is Hudas."
"16291","He said: Affan narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: Al-Numan ibn Salim informed me, he said: I heard Amr ibn Aws narrating from Abu Razin that he said: O Messenger of Allah, my father is a very old man unable to perform Hajj and Umrah or to travel. He said: Perform Hajj for your father and Umrah."
"16292","He said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us from Yala ibn Ata from Abu Razin Laqit from his uncle, raising it, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The dream of the believer is a part of forty parts of prophethood; I doubt that he said: The dream of the believer is upon the foot of a bird as long as he does not tell of it; when he tells of it, it occurs."
"16293","He said: Bahz narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Yala ibn Ata informed us from Waki ibn Hudas from his paternal uncle Abu Razin al-Uqayli that he said: O Messenger of Allah, will all of us see our Lord, Mighty and Majestic is He, on the Day of Resurrection, and what is the sign of that in His creation? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Does not each of you look at the moon alone with him? He said: Yes. He said: Then Allah is greater. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, how does Allah give life to the dead, and what is the sign of that in His creation? He said: Did you not pass by the valley of your people barren? He said: Yes. He said: Did you not pass by it shaking green? He said: I said: Yes. He said: Then you passed by it barren? He said: Yes. He said: Thus Allah gives life to the dead, and that is His sign in His creation."
"16294","He said: Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us from Yala ibn Ata from Waki ibn Hudas from Abu Razin, his uncle, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, how does Allah give life to the dead? He said: Did you not pass by the valley barren, then you pass by it green? Shubah said it more than twice: Thus Allah gives life to the dead."
"16295","He said: Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Abdullah, meaning Ibn al-Mubarak, informed us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir informed us from Sulayman ibn Musa from Abu Razin al-Uqayli, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, how does Allah give life to the dead? He said: Did you not pass by a barren land of your land, then you passed by it fertile? He said: Yes. He said: Thus is the resurrection. He said: O Messenger of Allah, what is faith? He said: That you testify that there is no god but Allah alone with no partner for Him, and that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger, and that Allah and His Messenger be dearer to you than others, and that being burned with fire be dearer to you than associating with Allah, and that you love one without kinship, loving him only for Allah, Mighty and Majestic is He. When you are so, the love of faith has entered your heart as the love of water enters the thirsty on a hot day. I said: O Messenger of Allah, how can I know that I am a believer? He said: No servant of my ummah, or this ummah, does a good deed and knows that it is good and that Allah, Mighty and Majestic is He, will reward him good for it, and does no evil deed but knows that it is evil and seeks the forgiveness of Allah, Mighty and Majestic is He, for it and knows that none forgives but He, except that he is a believer."
"16296","He said: Bahz narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: Yala ibn Ata informed me, he said: I heard Waki ibn Hudas narrating from his paternal uncle Abu Razin that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The dream of the Muslim is a part of forty parts of prophethood, and it is upon the foot of a bird as long as he does not speak of it; when he speaks of it, it occurs. He said: I think he said: Let him speak of it only to a beloved or an intelligent one."
"16297","He said: Abd al-Rahman and Ibn Jafar narrated to us, they said: Shubah narrated to us from Yala ibn Ata from Waki ibn Hudas from his paternal uncle Abu Razin, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, how does Allah give life to the dead? He said: Did you not pass by a barren valley, then you passed by it fertile? Ibn Jafar said: Then you pass by it green. He said: I said: Yes. He said: Thus Allah gives life to the dead."
"16298","He said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi and Bahz, the meaning, narrated to us, they said: Shubah narrated to us from Yala ibn Ata; Bahz said in his hadith, he said: Yala ibn Ata informed me, he said: I heard Waki ibn Hudas from his paternal uncle Abu Razin, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The dream of the believer is a part of forty parts of prophethood, and it is upon the foot of a bird as long as he does not speak of it; when he speaks of it, it drops. And I think he said: Let him speak of it only to a beloved or an intelligent one."
"16299","Abd al-Rahman and Bahz narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Yala ibn Ata from Waki ibn Udus from his paternal uncle Abu Razin; Bahz said: al-Uqayli, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah; Bahz said: Will all of us see our Lord, Mighty and Majestic is He? Abd al-Rahman said: How do we see our Lord on the Day of Resurrection, and what is the sign of that in His creation? So he said: Does not each of you look at the moon alone with him? He said: I said: Yes. He said: Then He is greater."
"16300","Bahz and Affan narrated to us, they said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: Al-Numan ibn Salim informed me, he said: I heard Amr ibn Aws, he said: Abu Razin said; Affan said in his hadith: from Abu Razin, that he said: O Messenger of Allah, my father is a very old man unable to bear Hajj or Umrah or travel. He said: Perform Hajj for your father and Umrah."
"16301","He said: Bahz narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Ya'la ibn 'Ata informed me, from Waki' ibn Hudus, from his uncle Abu Razin al-'Uqayli, that he said: O Messenger of Allah, where was our Lord, Mighty and Majestic, before He created the heavens and the earth? He said: In 'ama, above it there was no air and beneath it there was no air, then He created His Throne upon the water."
"16302","He said: Bahz and Hasan narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ya'la ibn 'Ata, from Waki' ibn Hudas, from his uncle Abu Razin, Hasan said: al-'Uqayli, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Our Lord laughs at the despair of His servant and the nearness of His relief. Abu Razin said: So I said: O Messenger of Allah, does the Lord, Mighty and Majestic, laugh? The Great? We shall never be deprived of good from a Lord who laughs. Hasan said in his hadith: So he said: Yes, we shall never be deprived of good from a Lord who laughs."
"16303","Bahz and 'Affan narrated to us, they said: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, he said: Ya'la ibn 'Ata narrated to us, from Waki' ibn Hudus al-'Uqayli, from his uncle Abu Razin, and he is Laqit ibn 'Amir, he said: Abu Razin informed me that he said: O Messenger of Allah, we used to slaughter in Rajab sacrifices, and we would eat from them and feed whoever came to us. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: There is no harm in that. He said: So Waki' said: I will never leave it ever."
"16304","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah informed us, from al-Nu'man ibn Salim, from 'Amr ibn Aws, from his uncle Abu Razin, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My father reached Islam while he is a very old shaykh, unable to perform Hajj nor 'Umrah nor traveling. He said: Perform Hajj on behalf of your father and perform 'Umrah."
"16305","Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Awanah informed us, from Ya'la ibn 'Ata, from Waki' ibn Hudas Abu Mus'ab al-'Uqayli, from his uncle Abu Razin, and he is Laqit ibn 'Amir ibn al-Muntafiq, he said: Abu Razin informed me that he said: O Messenger of Allah, we used to slaughter in Rajab sacrifices, and we would eat from them and feed whoever came to us. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no harm in that. So Waki' said: I will never leave it ever."
"16306","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: from Ya'la ibn 'Ata, from Waki' ibn Hudus, from Abu Razin, his uncle, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Muslim's dream is a part of forty parts of prophethood, and it is, meaning, on the leg of a bird, as long as he does not speak of it, and when he speaks of it, it occurs."
"16307","Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Hamzah ibn Muhammad ibn Hamzah ibn Mus'ab ibn al-Zubayr wrote to me: I have written to you this hadith, and I have presented it and compiled it according to what I have written to you, so narrate it on my authority. He said: Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mughirah al-Hizami narrated to me, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Ayyash al-Sam'i al-Ansari al-Quba'i, from Banu 'Amr ibn 'Awf, narrated to me, from Dalham ibn al-Aswad ibn Abdullah ibn Hajib ibn 'Amir ibn al-Muntafiq al-'Uqayli, from his father, from his uncle Laqit ibn 'Amir. Dalham said: And my father al-Aswad also narrated it to me, from 'Asim ibn Laqit, that Laqit went out as a delegate to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with a companion of his called Nahik ibn 'Asim ibn Malik ibn al-Muntafiq. Laqit said: So I went out, I and my companion, until we came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the end of Rajab, and we came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and found him when he had finished the morning prayer, and he stood among the people as a preacher and said: O people, indeed I have kept my voice from you for four days, so that I may make you hear; is there any man sent by his people who said: Learn for us what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) says; then perhaps the talk of his own soul distracts him, or the talk of his companion, or the misguided distract him; indeed I will be asked: Did I convey; listen, you shall live; sit, sit. He said: So the people sat, and I and my companion stood, until his heart and sight were free for us, I said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you have of the knowledge of the unseen? He laughed, by Allah, and shook his head, and knew that I was seeking his slip, and said: Your Lord, Mighty and Majestic, has withheld five keys of the unseen, none knows them but Allah, and he pointed with his hand. I said: What are they? He said: Knowledge of death, He has known the death of each one of you and you do not know it; and knowledge of the semen when it is in the womb, He has known it and you do not know; and He has known what is in tomorrow and what you will eat tomorrow and you do not know it; and He has known today the rain, you overlooking it, destitute, hopeful, fearful, and He remains laughing, He has known that your relief is near. Laqit said: We shall never be deprived of good from a Lord who laughs. And He has known the day of the Hour. I said: O Messenger of Allah, teach us from what you teach the people and what you know, for we are from a tribe whose attestation is not believed by anyone, from Madhhij who watch over us, and Khath'am who befriend us, and our clan from whom we are. He said: You shall remain as you remain, then your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) shall die, then you shall remain as you remain, then the Blast shall be sent, by your God, it shall not leave upon its back anything but it dies, and the angels who are with your Lord, Mighty and Majestic, then your Lord, Mighty and Majestic, shall come to survey the earth though the lands have become empty of Him, then your Lord, Mighty and Majestic, shall send the sky with rain from near the Throne, and by your God, it shall not leave upon its back any place where one slain fell nor burial place of a dead one but it shall split the grave open from him until it makes him at his head, and he sits upright, and your Lord says: Mahyam, for what he was in? He says: O Lord, yesterday, today, and for his recent acquaintance with life he thinks it is recent with his family. So I said: O Messenger of Allah, how shall He gather us after the winds and decay and beasts have torn us apart? He said: I inform you of the like of that in the favors of Allah: the earth, you looked upon it while it was dry, decayed clay, and you said: It shall never live; then your Lord, Mighty and Majestic, sent the sky upon it, and it did not remain but days until you looked upon it and it was one green expanse; and by your God, He is more able to gather them from water than to gather the vegetation of the earth, so they shall come out from the lowlands and from their places of death, and you shall look at Him and He shall look at you. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, how are we filling the earth while He is one Person, we look at Him and He looks at us? He said: I inform you of the like of that in the favors of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: the sun and the moon, a small sign from Him, you see them both and they both see you in one hour, you suffer no crowding in seeing them both; and by your God, He is more able to see you and that you see Him than that you see them both and they see you, you suffering no crowding in seeing them both. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what shall our Lord, Mighty and Majestic, do with us when we meet Him? He said: You shall be presented to Him, your pages open to Him, nothing hidden of you is hidden from Him, then your Lord, Mighty and Majestic, shall take with His Hand a handful of water and sprinkle your tribe with it, and by your God, not a drop of it shall miss the face of any one of you; as for the Muslim, it shall leave his face like the white garment, and as for the disbeliever, it shall brand him like black pitch. Then your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) shall leave, and the righteous shall separate upon his trail, and they shall traverse a bridge of the Fire, and one of you shall step on the ember and say: Hass; your Lord, Mighty and Majestic, says: Its time has come. Then you shall come upon the Hawd of the Messenger, upon the most thirsty drinking place, by Allah, never seen before; by your God, not one of you shall stretch his hand but a cup shall be placed upon it, purifying him from sweat and urine and filth; and the sun and the moon shall be withheld, and you shall not see either of them. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, by what shall we see? He said: With the like of your sight at this hour of yours, and that before sunrise, on a day when the earth shone and the mountains faced it. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, by what shall we be recompensed for our evil deeds and our good deeds? He said: The good deed for ten like it, and the evil deed for its like, except that He pardons. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, either Paradise or the Fire? He said: By your God, indeed the Fire has seven gates, there are no two gates of them but a rider travels between them seventy years; and indeed Paradise has eight gates, there are no two gates of them but a rider travels between them seventy years. I said: O Messenger of Allah, upon what shall we look from Paradise? He said: Upon rivers of pure honey, and rivers of a cup with no headache therein nor remorse, and rivers of milk whose taste has not changed, and water not stagnant, and fruit, by your God, such as you know, and better than its like with it, and purified spouses. I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we have therein spouses, or from among them righteous ones? He said: The righteous women for the righteous men, you shall enjoy them as your enjoyments in the world, and they shall enjoy you, except that there is no begetting. Laqit said: So I said: Has what we shall reach and end to been decreed? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not answer him. I said: O Messenger of Allah, upon what shall I pledge you? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stretched his hand and said: Upon establishing prayer, and giving zakah, and separating from the polytheist, and that you associate with Allah no other god. I said: And indeed for us is what is between the east and the west? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) withheld his hand and thought that I was stipulating something he would not give me. He said: I said: We shall settle of it wherever we wish, and no soul shall wrong except against itself. So he stretched his hand and said: That is for you, you shall settle wherever you wish, and none shall wrong against you except your own soul. He said: So we left him, then he said: Indeed these two, by your God, are among the most God-fearing of people in the first and the last. So Ka'b ibn al-Khudriyyah, one of Banu Bakr ibn Kilab, said to him: Who are they, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Banu al-Muntafiq, worthy of that. He said: So we left, and I turned to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, is there for anyone who passed away any good in their ignorance? He said: A man from the midst of Quraysh said: By Allah, indeed your father al-Muntafiq is in the Fire. He said: It was as if heat fell between my skin and my face and my flesh from what he said about my father before the people, and I intended to say: And your father, O Messenger of Allah, then the other was more ignorant, so I said: O Messenger of Allah, and your family? He said: And my family, by Allah, whenever you pass by the grave of an 'Amiri or Qurashi polytheist, say: Muhammad has sent me to you, and I give you glad tidings of what grieves you, you shall be dragged upon your face and your belly in the Fire. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what did that to them, though they were upon a deed they did only well, and they thought they were righteous? He said: That is because Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sent at the end of every seven nations, meaning a prophet, so whoever disobeyed his prophet was of the misguided, and whoever obeyed his prophet was of the guided."
